      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: s/monotonously/monotonically/\n\nNote that flash_log_dequeue_event() relies on the timestamp incrementing between log events.  That works with a monotonic counter, but is unlikely to be true with a 32-bit wall clock time.\n\nIf two events have the same timestamp, then looping with flash_log_dequeue_event() will skip the second event.\n\nI don\u0027t have a good way around that without adding more complexity, such as a variable-length encoding of a higher-bit-depth timestamp.  If you go that way, you could also use differential timestamps, which will yield a more efficient encoding because the delta between timestamps is likely \u003c32 bits.",
